  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8909a7b854c460945b7273a620ed017e, type: 3}
  m_Name: PoI_01_Susan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: Storyteller
  characterAvatar: {fileID: 0}
  arrivalPrompt: You have arrived at the site.
  arrivalButtonText: Start
  dialogueLines:
  - My name is Susan. I grew up and live in Christchurch.
  - Standing here in Cathedral Square today... The Cathedral tower and spire are
    missing, but they hold a special place in my memory. They been the easiest way
    to find my way around Christchurch. You could see it from so many places in the
    town.
  - "When I was at school, I got lost around Cathedral Square during a school trip.
    I remember my teacher, Mr Watson, once told us: 'If you are lost, look for the
    Cathedral spire\u2014it's the tallest building in the town!'  I heard the bell,
    looked up, and found my way back."
  - "The last time I saw the spire, I was visiting the square with my homestay student.
    Now, when I pass by here, I still see the absence of that spire. I always try
    to look up as I used to, and I outline its contours in my mind \u2014 it's a
    habit that never left me."
  - Even when I wasn't standing right beside it, knowing where the cathedral was
    helped me feel oriented in the city. I suppose it was always part of how I remembered
    Christchurch...
  alignmentPrompt: Position yourself to match the historical perspective.
  alignmentButtonText: I'm in Position
  interactionInstruction: 
  interactionButtonText: Got it
  reflectionPrompt: Take a moment to reflect on what you've just experienced.
  reflectionButtonText: Continue
